            <ArticleTitle>A stimulator for studies of mechanical nociception based upon a commercially available translation table.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>199-204</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We have developed a mechanical stimulator that can be used for studies of sensory physiology, psychophysics and tissue mechanics. The stimulator operates in either displacement or force-servo modes. It surpasses other available stimulators in respect to displacement range, measurement sensitivity and cost, and it can be easily assembled from parts that are commercially available.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
